DESCRIPTION:This MAP Session is the second for the 26-27 year. In this ses
 sion\, MAP is partnering with The Career Exploration & Student Employment
  Center to learn about building a successful resume. Come and learn how t
 o put your best foot forward with your resume!\nThe Mentor Apprenticeship
  Program (MAP) is a two-semester training series facilitated by the FASE 
 Mentoring Program. It gives students at IU Bloomington opportunities to e
 nhance their mentoring\, teamwork\, and leadership skills. Upon completio
 n of MAP\, students receive a Certificate of Completion\, which establish
 es their commitment to growth and leadership.\nAll Indiana University eve
 nts\, groups\, activities\, and educational\, cultural\, and historical o
 bservances welcome all IU students and other members of the Indiana Unive
 rsity community.\n\nHosted by: Mentoring Services and Leadership Developm
 ent \n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://beinvolved.indian
 a.edu/event/12517882
DTEND:20261007T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260730T032053Z
DTSTART:20261006T230000Z
