DESCRIPTION:This MAP Session is the third session for the 26-27 year. In t
 his session\, MAP is partnering with Counseling And Psychological Service
 s (CAPS) to learn about burnout\, how it affects student leaders differen
 tly\, and how we can prevent it. Learn strategies to help you be the best
  leader you can be!\nThe Mentor Apprenticeship Program (MAP) is a two-sem
 ester training series facilitated by the FASE Mentoring Program. It gives
  students at IU Bloomington opportunities to enhance their mentoring\, te
 amwork\, and leadership skills. Upon completion of MAP\, students receive
  a Certificate of Completion\, which establishes their commitment to grow
 th and leadership.\nAll Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\,
  and educational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all IU s
 tudents and other members of the Indiana University community.\n\nHosted 
 by: Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS)\, Mentoring Services and
  Leadership Development \n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https
 ://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12517601
DTEND:20261111T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260730T032053Z
DTSTART:20261104T000000Z
